# CODEOWNERS
#
# GitHub requests a review from the owners listed here on every pull request
# that touches a matching path. With "Require review from Code Owners" turned
# on in the branch protection rule (or ruleset) for `main`, a pull request
# cannot merge until a code owner approves it.
#
# Rules:
# - The LAST matching pattern wins, so the catch-all comes first and the
#   more specific, security-sensitive paths come after it.
# - Every owner must be a user or team with write access, or GitHub ignores
#   the line. Use real handles only; never add bots or placeholder names.
# - Sensitive paths are listed explicitly even though they share the
#   default owner today. That way, adding a co-maintainer to the catch-all
#   later does not quietly let them approve changes to CI, releases,
#   dependencies or the redaction code on their own.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default owner for everything
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                   @raulkivi

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repository governance: who can approve what, and the security policy.
# Owning CODEOWNERS itself stops a pull request from removing its own
# required reviewers.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @raulkivi
/SECURITY.md                        @raulkivi
/CONTRIBUTING.md                    @raulkivi
/LICENSE                            @raulkivi
/docs/threat-model.md               @raulkivi

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI/CD and automation: workflows run with repository tokens and publishing
# secrets, so any change here is a supply-chain risk.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/workflows/                 @raulkivi
/.github/dependabot.yml             @raulkivi

# Agent instructions steer the AI reviewers and coding agents that run on PRs.
/.github/copilot-instructions.md    @raulkivi
/.github/instructions/              @raulkivi
/CLAUDE.md                          @raulkivi
/.claude/                           @raulkivi

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies and build configuration: new or changed packages, install
# scripts and lockfile edits.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
package.json                        @raulkivi
/package-lock.json                  @raulkivi
/scripts/                           @raulkivi

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Release and publishing of the VS Code extension (Marketplace / Open VSX).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/packages/vscode-extension/package.json   @raulkivi
/packages/vscode-extension/scripts/       @raulkivi

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Code that handles sensitive local data: redaction of captured traffic and
# tool output, security detectors, and the MCP server exposed to agents.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/packages/server/src/data-sources/log-providers/mitmproxy/   @raulkivi
/packages/server/src/services/tool-audit/                    @raulkivi
/packages/server/src/services/insights/                      @raulkivi
